164d|n|To descend; to light. ; To burst forth or dart, as lightning; to shine with, or like, lightning; to display a flash or flashes of lightning; to flash. ; To grow lighter; to become less dark or lowering; to brighten; to clear, as the sky. ; To make light or clear; to light; to illuminate; as, to lighten an apartment with lamps or gas; to lighten the streets. ; To illuminate with knowledge; to enlighten. ; To emit or disclose in, or as in, lightning; to flash out, like lightning. ; To free from trouble and fill with joy. ; To make lighter, or less heavy; to reduce in weight; to relieve of part of a load or burden; as, to lighten a ship by unloading; to lighten a load or burden. ; To make less burdensome or afflictive; to alleviate; as, to lighten the cares of life or the burden of grief. ; To cheer; to exhilarate.	V:84k,100,1~84k,100,1
