1674|n|A thong by which a dog is led; a leash. ; The linden tree. See Linden. ; A fruit allied to the lemon, but much smaller; also, the tree which bears it. There are two kinds; Citrus Medica, var. acida which is intensely sour, and the sweet lime (C. Medica, var. Limetta) which is only slightly sour. ; Birdlime. ; Oxide of calcium; the white or gray, caustic substance, usually called quicklime, obtained by calcining limestone or shells, the heat driving off carbon dioxide and leaving lime. It develops great heat when treated with water, forming slacked lime, and is an essential ingredient of cement, plastering, mortar, etc.	a:1x9g,105,2;200i,77,2;1op7,30,1~1x9g,105,2;200i,77,2;1op7,30,1	v:1x9g,105,2;26ev,6,3~26ev,6,3;1x9g,105,2	n:1op7,30,1;1649,30,2~1649,30,2;1op7,30,1	N:140e,92,3;28bf,91,1;vs8,48,2;dvr,28,1~140e,92,3;vs8,48,2;28bf,91,1;dvr,28,1
